    "limits": "Each Before/After helper owns at most its exact perAPI inlinePOD, source source-scalar scratch and stated256Bhashstate. Helper returns before original delegate, so BeforePOD is NOT retained across nested originals; only Token48+Admission24 (72bytes) wrapperlocals may spanoriginal. At most32trackedactivewrappers; unselected wrapper stillretains constanttoken/admissionlocals but no implied globalcallback/threadmemorycap. Afterhelper uses same max704 independently after originalreturn. Actual compilerstack/spills/threadTLS/foreignlibraries not sizeof-bounded here; future compilation/lifetimeproof gate.",
    "SOURCE_entry_inline_POD_bytes": 56,
    "tracked_wrapper_tokens_admissions_total_bytes": 2304,
    "no_borrow_across_original": "A SOURCE helper may have SourceEntryInput56 plus Token/Admission caller spans; it returns before the original. Typed Before helper1448 maximum and After helper704 maximum have disjoint lifetimes. Before/After/Entry inline PODs are NOT retained in each nested wrapper; only32*(Token48+Admission24)=2304B across tracked originals, plus at most one metadata-helper POD at a time on the single selected thread. RootParse24 and source digest256 are separate stated maxima. C actual call frames/alignment/spills remain unmeasured; no stack/totalCPU assertion."
