  "no_report_or_execution_envelope": "No C model report, hex BEFORE/AFTER execution envelope or old512KiB envelope is allocated/admitted. Only raw UTF8 frame<=65536; model report262144 remains external pure-model cap.",
  "arena_representation": "One typed context struct with members in arena_sections order: osw_context_header_v1 header; typedRecordSlot records[64]; osw_pending_v1 pending[32]; osw_identity_v1 identity[21]; osw_aliasslot_v1 aliases[8]; uint8_t serializer_workspace[65536]; uint8_t immutable_payload[65536]. Natural alignment8; no chararena effective-type casts.",
  "core_issuer_bytes_separate": 64,
  "new_core_total_static_bytes_PROPOSED": 404416,
  "issuer_scope": "One64Bissuer static in loaded NEWcore, not one pertestcontext or shader/forwarder. Production exactlyone context; future isolatedCPU contexts use sameissuer for crosscontexttests. Monotone checkednonzero context/run/owner/thread identifiers; never reused within THIS loadedcore lifetime. No interprocess/multipleloadedcore/reload uniqueness/authorization claim. Context epoch1/noreset; ContextCookie unique fromissuer.",
  "no_hidden_pools": "No second root/after/PODcache, objectmap, TLSstack or pendingperfamily arenas. ActiveStack32 and immutable snapshot are insideheader; scalar pending notes in128Bslots; originaltyped snapshots in64typedrecords only. MetadataJSONserialization/digest use statedworkspace/state. Runtime/compileroriginal allocations are outside this proposed observerstorage and not totalCPUbounded.",
  "counter_authority": "Only CoreIssuer counters allocate IDs; each next_* field holds HIGHEST ISSUED checkedU64value, initially0, then checked+1 allocation. Header.next_owner_id and PublicStatus.next_alias_id are diagnostic CACHES of the highest owner counter observed from that issuer, initially0. They are NEVER local allocators, never a promise about the next returned alias. No local increment or raw token reuse.",
  "atomic_backend": "Proposed GCC/Clang __atomic operations on naturally aligned private uint32_t try_lock/terminal_reason/flags (and issuer lock/flags) fields. No cast to a differently laid out _Atomic type, no atomicstruct/flexiblearray assumption. All concurrent accesses to a shared latch are atomic; regular context mutations happen under trylock. Four-byte lock/latch operations must be verified lockfree on future pinned target compilers; ABI/stack/link not measured here.",
  "header_private_closure_semantics": {
    "active_stack": "At most32 pending indices, parent/depth references index same32slots, no per-family/extra TLS stacks.",
    "generation_counters": "12kind counters indexed kindtag-1; initially0, reservechecked+1 at actualcreatorENTRY; holes onfailedcreates allowed. Never generated from RETURN or outputrawnumerology.",
    "snapshot_capture_and_ticket": "Copied once at actualselectedExecuteRETURN; pendingatboundary immutable, currentlive_drain_pending separate. No extra record/root caches.",
